<h1>treesort (1)</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a> algorithm that first builds a <a href="binarySearchTree.html"><em>binary search tree</em></a> of the <a href="key.html"><em>keys</em></a>, then accesses the keys with an <a href="inorderTraversal.html"><em>in-order traversal</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="sort.html"><em>sort</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate child</strong> (... is a part of or used in me.)<br>
<a href="binarySearchTree.html"><em>binary search tree</em></a>, <a href="inorderTraversal.html"><em>in-order traversal</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="blindSort.html"><em>blind sort</em></a>, <a href="treesort2.html"><em>treesort (2)</em></a>, <a href="heapSort.html"><em>heapsort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
For good performance, use a <a href="balancedbist.html"><em>balanced binary search tree</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/4/426.treesort.p" target="_blank">(C)</a>
